        "answer": "# Nuclear Fission\n\nNuclear fission is a neutron-induced nuclear reaction where a heavy nucleus, like **uranium-235**, breaks into two intermediate mass nuclear fragments when bombarded with a neutron .\n\nFor example, when a uranium-235 isotope is bombarded with a neutron, it can break into barium and krypton, releasing additional neutrons and a significant amount of energy .\n\nThe energy released in a fission reaction of nuclei like uranium is typically around **200 MeV per fissioning nucleus** . This energy initially appears as the kinetic energy of the fragments and neutrons, eventually transferring to the surroundings as heat . Nuclear fission is the energy source in nuclear reactors for electricity generation and the enormous energy released in an atom bomb .\n\n**📘 Source:** NCERT Class 12 Physics • Nuclear Fission"
